# CI Builder — 9 modules / 52 sub-modules (Aug 2026)

Canonical catalog: `lib/ci-builder/modules-catalog.ts` (from `lib/sow/CI Builder Modules - for cursor.csv`).

## Model

- Each `ci_sections` row = one **sub-module** (`section_type` = catalog id, e.g. `mission`, `primary_logo`, `color_primary`).
- 9 modules: Brand Core, Voice & AI, Logo, Colors, Typography, Design Tokens, UI Elements, Imagery, Touchpoints.
- Legacy 11 types (`overview`, `logo`, `colors`, …) still render via old section components for existing guidelines.
- Unmatched Figma frames → Unassigned Assets pool (no hard crash).

## 4-column contract

- Admin edit: `SubModuleSection` + primitives (`EditableText/Image/Color/ListItem`)
- Client **Presentation** vs **Elements** toggle: `/g/[slug]` `PublicGuidelineClient`
- Copy Prompt: catalog `promptTemplate` via `lib/ci-builder/prompts.ts`

## Key paths

- Catalog / defaults: `lib/ci-builder/modules-catalog.ts`
- Glossary / Figma match: `lib/ci-builder/glossary.ts`
- Renderer: `components/ci-builder/sections/SubModuleSection.tsx` + `sections/index.tsx`
- Admin add: `AdminEditor` → “Add Sub-Module” grouped by module
- Seed data: `defaultDataForSubModule` / `figma/normalize/helpers.ts`

## Next polish (if needed)

- Deepen per-submodule elements downloads (woff2, zip, CMYK overrides)
- Map Figma CSS/Variables import into color_/type_/layout_/spacing_ slots more precisely
- Optional “seed all 52” on new guideline
